trix}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+CB & =(A+C)B \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-2B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186235392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83e8b5b8-2dc6-502f-9895-61592963799f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186234745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83e8b5b8-2dc6-502f-9895-61592963799f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186234745} :answer-field/id #uuid "73f19ed8-00ca-518c-b9b0-9aa8b5d98ca5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186235100} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3d714a7-0082-5d4f-ab9a-17597b16c336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186234904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3d714a7-0082-5d4f-ab9a-17597b16c336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186234904} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eddebdf-1405-58bc-9c0f-2eb87f83aa52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186235144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c56147c9-f2b7-5667-be10-7a59be78f3d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186234854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56147c9-f2b7-5667-be10-7a59be78f3d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186234854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d733dbe9-c554-5e94-95f1-066ae833b632" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186235234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd65aedc-568a-52b0-80dd-3058db6f72f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186234893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd65aedc-568a-52b0-80dd-3058db6f72f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186234893} :answer-field/id #uuid "f602e10d-959a-555e-a86b-ac99268e9349" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186235267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27a916f2-ae5e-57d0-a97a-ec9cecb80707" :question/math-academy-id "q-138783" :question/problem "$$\nX+Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ+YZ=(X+Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ+YZ \\\\  & =(X+Y)Z \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186265870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #u